# tally 2.2.1 (#219, 219.2), L §5.19 l.1717: "Where the two rows disagree on an amount or a day, each end is booked as
# its own statement says, WARN-LEGS is printed": bank[a2] and sbank[b1], stated same and fulfilling nothing, disagree
# (950.00 and 900.00 PLN), so the run warns, the movement named by its first row. tally 2.2 warned only for rows that
# fulfil an instance (the review's s5/r3_disagree.tally).
=== r3.tally
model r3
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-30
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-04-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place sav: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed
input sbank: observed

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 2000.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
  opening[sav] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"

version st_konto
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-02
  covers konto
  bank[a2] = (on: 2026-03-18, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to sav amount 950.00 PLN) "konto line 2"

version st_sav
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-05
  covers sav
  sbank[b1] = (on: 2026-03-18, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to sav amount 900.00 PLN) "sav line 1"

version link
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-04-20
  same bank[a2] = sbank[b1]

ask a_before: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(sav, 2026-03-31), count(m in transfers over 2026-03), flows(sav, 2026-03) as known 2026-04-01
ask b_on1: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(sav, 2026-03-31), count(m in transfers over 2026-03), flows(sav, 2026-03) as known 2026-04-02
ask c_between: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(sav, 2026-03-31), count(m in transfers over 2026-03), flows(sav, 2026-03) as known 2026-04-03
ask d_on2: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(sav, 2026-03-31), count(m in transfers over 2026-03), flows(sav, 2026-03) as known 2026-04-05
ask e_after: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(sav, 2026-03-31), count(m in transfers over 2026-03), flows(sav, 2026-03)
ask f_amt: sum(m.cash.amount for m in transfers over 2026-03)
ask g_amt_mid: sum(m.cash.amount for m in transfers over 2026-03) as known 2026-04-03
=== expect
a_before: (2 000.00 PLN, 0.00 PLN, 0, 0.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-04-01
b_on1: (1 050.00 PLN, 950.00 PLN, 1, 950.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-04-02
c_between: (1 050.00 PLN, 950.00 PLN, 1, 950.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-04-03
d_on2: (1 050.00 PLN, 900.00 PLN, 1, 900.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-04-05
e_after: (1 050.00 PLN, 900.00 PLN, 1, 900.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-04-30
f_amt: ?"bank[a2] and sbank[b1] are one, but the amount of cash differs on 2026-03-18: 950.00 PLN (bank[a2]) and 900.00 PLN (sbank[b1])" (bank[a2], sbank[b1])
  cut 2026-04-30
g_amt_mid: 950.00 PLN
  cut 2026-04-03
warning: WARN-LEGS the two observations of bank[a2] disagree: bank[a2] (950.00 PLN) and sbank[b1] (900.00 PLN)
warning: WARN-UNREAD place world is read by nothing
